 "drivingQuestion": "Why does R' Yosei permit renting houses but not fields in EY?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "avodah_zarah.21a.9",
   "daf": "21a",
   "sentenceId": 8,
   "he": "רַבִּי יוֹסֵי אוֹמֵר: בְּאֶרֶץ יִשְׂרָאֵל מַשְׂכִּירִין לָהֶם בָּתִּים וְכוּ׳. מַאי טַעְמָא? שָׂדוֹת דְּאִית בְּהוּ תַּרְתֵּי — גְּזַרוּ בְּהוּ רַבָּנַן, בָּתִּים דְּלֵית בְּהוּ תַּרְתֵּי — לָא גְּזַרוּ בְּהוּ רַבָּנַן.",
   "en": "The mishna further teaches that «Rabbi Yosei says: In Eretz Yisrael one may rent houses» but not fields «to» gentiles. The Gemara explains: «What is the reason» that one may rent houses but not fields? «Concerning fields, which have two» problems, «the Sages issued a decree» as a preventive measure prohibiting the renting of fields in Eretz Yisrael. But «concerning houses, which do not have two» problems, «the Sages did not issue a decree» prohibiting renting houses to gentiles."
  }
 ],
